+# Checkpoint R3 independent acceptance — Sol LOW
+
+VERDICT: PASS (r3)
+
+Checker: Codex Sol, LOW effort. Independent read-only validation of the maker's checkpoint at HEAD `06acb7f4f377a21e4cb2f6b3d712de23170cad30`; only this report was added. No model server, inference, benchmark, performance, latency, or Vulkan run was performed. I did not infer the served OOM root cause.
+
+LENS: checkpoint R3 correctness and release-safety acceptance
+FINDINGS:
+NONE
+CHECKED:
+1. Dedicated explicit option, default OFF and independent of dev/tests — read `CMakeLists.txt:25-30` and `src/CMakeLists.txt:61-72`. `LLAMA_TEST_CHECKPOINT_FAULT_INJECTION` is one top-level option with literal default `OFF`; the only CMake definition of `LLAMA_TEST_FAULT_INJECTION` is inside `if (LLAMA_TEST_CHECKPOINT_FAULT_INJECTION)`, with no `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV` or `LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS` dependency.
+2. Current default/tests-enabled build excludes the seam — `build-checker-r3-default/CMakeCache.txt` binds the build to this exact worktree and records `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV=ON`, `LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=ON`, and `LLAMA_TEST_CHECKPOINT_FAULT_INJECTION=OFF`; its `compile_commands.json` has zero `LLAMA_TEST_FAULT_INJECTION` occurrences. A fresh `cmake --build ... --parallel 1` dependency check completed with exit 0 and rebuilt only generated UI assets, establishing that the compiled checkpoint objects and binaries remain current with the present source/configuration. The default test and server binaries each contain zero `LLAMA_R46_CKPT_FAIL_*` strings. With `LLAMA_R46_CKPT_FAIL_ALLOC=1` set externally, a fresh default-binary run explicitly reported Test 11 `SKIPPED` because the seam was not compiled and passed both attention models (`2 passed, 0 failed`); the ordinary tests-enabled binary cannot respond to that checkpoint-injection environment variable.
+3. Current explicit fault-test build includes the seam — the otherwise-identical `build-checker-r3-inject` cache records `LLAMA_TEST_CHECKPOINT_FAULT_INJECTION=ON`, and its compile database contains 394 propagated `LLAMA_TEST_FAULT_INJECTION` occurrences. A fresh serial dependency build completed with exit 0 and rebuilt only generated UI assets. Its test and server binaries contain four and two checkpoint-injection strings respectively, and fresh test output stated that the seam was compiled and then observed deterministic allocation and copy failures.
+4. Both macro states compile — fresh serial dependency builds of `llama`, `test-save-load-state`, `test-recurrent-state-rollback`, `test-ctx-checkpoint-storage`, `llama-server`, and `llama-speculative-simple` exited 0 in both directories. No checkpoint source needed recompilation, which ties the existing artifacts to the current dependency graph without duplicating the expired checker's builds.
+5. Fallible finalization and failure propagation — read `src/llama-context.cpp:3249-3360,3640-3691`, `common/common.h:1255-1272`, and `common/common.cpp:2382-2442`. Device finalization occurs inside the save exception boundary, returns zero on failure, erases a newly-created storage entry, and scrubs the serialized output. The common checkpoint helpers are `[[nodiscard]] bool`; `git grep` found nine call sites and every one checks the result. Both affected application targets compiled in both macro states.
+6. Prior checkpoint preservation and zero-byte safety — read the off-map allocate/copy/publish sequence at `src/llama-context.cpp:3280-3356` and symmetric zero-size skips at `:3290-3317,3408-3444`. Publication is a single move after every allocation/copy succeeds; zero-byte entries create no tensor, buffer, or backend copy. Injected Test 11 passed the first-save failure, replacement allocation failure, replacement copy failure, retry, storage independence, and nonempty-header/zero-device-byte round-trip legs.
+7. Architecture-independent injected tests — fresh serial explicit-seam runs passed Llama dense and MoE (`2 passed, 0 failed`), Mamba recurrent (`1 passed, 0 failed`), and Jamba hybrid (`1 passed, 0 failed`). Each displayed the Test 11 banner, the seam-present statement, deterministic allocation and copy failure logs, and final `PASS`; the tests do not depend on checkpoint byte-size changes.
+8. Exact storage-ID behavior — read `tests/test-save-load-state.cpp:866-1261`; storage IDs 1-4 are explicit, storage 3 is seeded, failed, and restored using `fl3` and its own control, storage 2 retries independently, and storage 1 remains intact. A fresh `test-ctx-checkpoint-storage` run exited 0 with `PASS (0 failures)`.
+9. Source/report integrity — read `OPUS-CHECKPOINT-R3-PROMPT.md`, `OPUS-CHECKPOINT-R3-REPORT.md`, `CHECK-CHECKPOINT-R2-SOL-LOW.md`, the current diffs for all nine modified code paths, the relevant finalization/read/write code, the full Test 11 body, and every `update_tgt/update_dft` caller. Current SHA-256 values were recorded during the check for the load-bearing files (`CMakeLists.txt` `2E228C69...995B3`, `src/CMakeLists.txt` `EB65BCCD...577D2`, `src/llama-context.cpp` `FA1994FB...D8C1`, `tests/test-save-load-state.cpp` `95F4A7A8...1D44`, `tests/test-recurrent-state-rollback.cpp` `AB0F34CB...52121`). R3 changes are confined to the requested CMake guard, seam comment, and test presence/absence messages/helper placement; the R2 transaction and caller behavior remains intact. `git diff --check` exited 0.
+NOT CHECKABLE: Runtime server fallback behavior was source-checked and compiled but not executed because server runs were forbidden. The second-buffer-type injection leg cannot be exercised on the available CPU-only backend and was explicitly reported `NOT EXERCISED`; it was not counted as passing coverage.
