+# Opus maker task: checkpoint finalization safety R2
+
+Read `CHECK-CHECKPOINT-R1-SOL.md` in full. Work in `C:/ArifiLabs/cache/hq57-checkpoint-wt`. You own:
+
+- `src/llama-context.cpp` and existing checkpoint tests
+- `common/common.cpp` and its declaration header if required
+- `tools/server/server-context.cpp` only for the checked failed-save propagation/drop path
+- test/CMake files only if required
+- `OPUS-CHECKPOINT-R2-REPORT.md`
+
+Do not run model inference/serving, benchmarks, performance/latency/bandwidth measurements, alter scheduled tasks, commit, or touch Vulkan allocator policy/kernels. Builds and generated tiny dummy-model correctness tests are allowed.
+
+Repair every Sol finding:
+
+1. No map mutation in the fallible prepare phase: never use `mbufs[buft]` before success. A first-save allocation failure must leave no entry; restore then returns failure/0 without any GGML_ABORT.
+2. Preserve every previous valid checkpoint byte-for-byte until the complete replacement succeeds. Do not REFRESH/REUSE a live buffer in place. Prepare new contexts/buffers/tensors off-map for every replacement, perform all copies there, then publish all buffer types only after every allocation/copy succeeds. Accept the explicit old+new peak and document it.
+3. Eliminate fallible `ggml_tallocr_alloc` paths that abort on exhaustion. Every injected allocation/placement/copy failure must return 0 through the save boundary. No destructor throw/abort/null-backed copy.
+4. Handle zero-byte buffer/tensor groups without allocating or invoking backend copy/set on null buffers. Define and test their successful no-op representation and restore behavior.
+5. Propagate save failure through `common_prompt_checkpoint::update_tgt/update_dft` without GGML_ABORT. Return a status and have server checkpoint creation refuse/drop the incomplete entry or safely fall back according to the actual ownership design. No retry loop, false success, or later invalid restore.
+6. Make tests architecture-independent. Do not assume 40 to 60 tokens changes checkpoint bytes on recurrent caches. Seed and verify the exact storage ID being failed/retried/restored, including storage 3 in the former Test E. Exercise first and replacement allocation/copy failure, multi-buffer failure, zero-byte, retry, partial flags, dense/MoE and recurrent Mamba/RWKV shapes where available.
+7. Correct the R1 report's invalid old-code RED claim in the new report. The old code lacks the env injection seam. Prove the current negative seam is live with deterministic current-code failures and paired clean controls; do not claim a historical allocator assertion you did not execute.
+8. Inspect whether the environment injection seam is reachable in production builds; constrain it to test/debug builds if the build system supports a reliable compile guard, or explicitly justify a safe deterministic test seam that cannot be accidentally enabled on a served release.
+
+Build serially in the existing isolated checker build if sound, otherwise a new isolated build directory. Run focused save/load tests on generated Llama dense/MoE and Mamba dummy models, plus any direct zero-byte probe. Run `git diff --check`. Report exact commands/results, caller behavior, peak-memory tradeoff and remaining limits. Stop without commit.
