@@ -0,0 +1,186 @@
+# Checkpoint R3 — release-safe fault-injection seam
+
+Maker: Opus 5. Scope: the single R2 blocking finding (CHECK-CHECKPOINT-R2-SOL-LOW.md finding 1,
+mandate 8). No transaction or caller behavior was changed. No inference, server, benchmark, latency,
+scheduled-task, or Vulkan work was performed. Nothing was committed.
+
+## The blocker
+
+`src/CMakeLists.txt` defined `LLAMA_TEST_FAULT_INJECTION` whenever `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV` was ON, and
+root `CMakeLists.txt:14` defaults that option ON. An ordinary source-built `llama-server` therefore
+compiled the `LLAMA_R46_CKPT_FAIL_ALLOC` / `_COPY` environment reads unless the builder remembered
+`-DLLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV=OFF`.
+
+## The fix
+
+| File | Change |
+|---|---|
+| `CMakeLists.txt` | New `option(LLAMA_TEST_CHECKPOINT_FAULT_INJECTION ... OFF)`, declared at top level, outside any `LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS` or `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV` block |
+| `src/CMakeLists.txt` | The seam definition is gated on that option **alone**; `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV` is no longer consulted. Definition stays `PUBLIC` so the library and the tests can never disagree about whether the seam exists. Both branches emit a `message(STATUS "checkpoint fault-injection seam: ON/OFF")` |
+| `src/llama-context.cpp` | Comment corrected — it claimed the macro was tied to `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV` |
+| `tests/test-save-load-state.cpp` | The Test 11 skip message names the new option and the exact repair command, and states that the test claims **no** coverage in that build. The seam-present branch logs that it was built with the option ON. `ckpt_fail_env` moved inside the `#ifdef` (its only callers are there; seam-OFF is now the default compile path) |
+
+The option is independent of `LLAMA_BUILD_IS_DEV` and `LLAMA_BUILD_TESTS` and defaults OFF in every
+build. A dev build, a release build, and a build with tests enabled all compile the constant-false
+`llama_io_ckpt_fail_at` body and no environment read.
+
+Skip-path behavior is unchanged in kind: Test 11 still returns `true` when the seam is absent, so a
+default `-DLLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=ON` suite stays green while refusing to claim the coverage.
+
+## Evidence
+
+Two fresh build directories, identical except for the one option. Ninja, Release, static, CPU only:
+
+```
+cmake -S . -B build-r3-default -G Ninja -DLLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=ON -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF \
+      -DGGML_CUDA=OFF -DGGML_VULKAN=OFF -DGGML_HIP=OFF -DGGML_NATIVE=OFF -DLLAMA_CURL=OFF \
+      -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=-D_WIN32_WINNT=0x0A00
+
+cmake -S . -B build-r3-inject  -G Ninja -DLLAMA_BUILD_TESTS=ON -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF \
