+| Leg | Injection | Asserted |
+|---|---|---|
+| A | ALLOC=1 on a first save into storage 1 | returns 0, no crash, no false success |
+| A2 | none | the immediate retry saves in full |
+| B | ALLOC=1 on a replacement (40-cell image, 60-cell state) | returns 0 AND storage 1 still restores byte-identical to the host control |
+| C | COPY=1 on the same replacement | returns 0 AND storage 1 still restores byte-identical |
+| D | COPY=1 on a first save into storage 2, then a clean retry | returns 0, retry saves and restores correctly, storage 1 still intact (no aliased/shared state between ids) |
+| E | ALLOC=2 | second buffer type of one finalization. On a single-buffer-type device attempt 2 is never reached and the save must be COMPLETE; where it is reached the save must return 0 and storage 1 must still restore. Both outcomes are checked — the leg never silently passes |
+| F | none | a clean `PARTIAL_ONLY` save/restore on storage 3 after all injected failures (byte count only: a partial image legitimately differs from the full host control on SWA archs) |
